            <h1>Double Trolley Overhead Cranes: High-Efficiency Handling and Versatile Applications</h1>
            <p>The double trolley overhead cranes are a special type of overhead cranes that feature two independently operated trolleys. Each trolley is typically equipped with a lifting hook or other lifting device, which can operate simultaneously or independently. This design makes the crane ideal for work scenarios that require handling multiple heavy objects at the same time, such as assembly lines in large factories or shipbuilding yards.</p>
            <p>Depending on the type of lifting mechanism, the double trolley overhead cranes can be classified into two types: the winch type and the hoist type. Each type has its own unique design and advantages, making them suitable for different application scenarios.</p><p>Depending on the type of lifting mechanism, the double trolley overhead cranes can be classified into two types: the winch type and the hoist type. Each type has its own unique design and advantages, making them suitable for different application scenarios.</p><p>Depending on the type of lifting mechanism, the double trolley overhead cranes can be classified into two types: the winch type and the hoist type. Each type has its own unique design and advantages, making them suitable for different application scenarios.</p>
