            <h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="crane1">Double Winches Overhead Cranes</h2>
            <p>The winch-type double trolley overhead cranes are commonly used in places that require lifting and moving heavy objects, such as steel mills, ports, and shipyards. It is suitable for high-frequency, heavy-load lifting tasks.</p>
            <figure class="wp-block-image size-full">
              <img decoding="async" width="2560" height="1706" src="/media/double-trolley/double-winch-overhead-crane-scaled.jpg" alt="double winch overhead crane scaled" class="wp-image-10791" />
            </figure>
            <div style="height:50px" aria-hidden="true" class="wp-block-spacer"></div>
            <h3 class="wp-block-heading">Features</h3>
            <ul class="wp-block-list"><li>Lifting Mechanism: The winch-type double girder overhead crane uses a winch as its main lifting mechanism. The winch is driven by an electric motor, which winds the steel rope around a drum to lift and lower heavy loads.</li><li>Heavy Load Capacity: Due to the large power output and strong pulling force of the winch, this type of crane is typically suitable for lifting heavy loads, such as in steel mills, shipyards, and heavy machinery manufacturing plants.</li><li>High Stability: The winch-type crane has a more robust structure, making it better able to handle high-intensity and high-frequency operations, particularly excelling in lifting and transporting super-heavy items.</li><li>Ease of Maintenance: The maintenance of the winch is relatively easy due to its simpler structure, lower failure rate, and ease of repairing or replacing parts.</li><li>Ease of Maintenance: The maintenance of the winch is relatively easy due to its simpler structure, lower failure rate, and ease of repairing or replacing parts.</li><li>1111111</li><li>我新加入</li></ul>
