            <h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="crane2">Double Hoists Overhead Cranes</h2>
            <p>The hoist-type double trolley overhead cranes are commonly used in environments such as warehouses, workshops, logistics centers, and assembly lines, where frequent handling is required but heavy loads are not necessary. It is also suitable for lifting needs with lower heights and smaller spans.</p>
            <figure class="wp-block-image size-full">
              <img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1194" height="793" src="/media/double-trolley/Double-Hoists-Trolley-Overhead-Cranes.jpg" alt="Double Hoists Trolley Overhead Cranes" class="wp-image-10810" />
            </figure>
            <div style="height:50px" aria-hidden="true" class="wp-block-spacer"></div>
            <h3 class="wp-block-heading">Features</h3>
            <ul class="wp-block-list">
              <li>Lifting Mechanism: The hoist-type double trolley overhead crane uses an electric hoist as its lifting mechanism. The electric hoist drives the hook via a chain or steel rope to lift and lower materials.</li>
              <li>Light to Medium Load Applications: Compared to winch-type cranes, hoist-type cranes are more suitable for light to medium load applications, typically used for handling and loading/unloading relatively lighter items.</li>
              <li>Easy Operation: The electric hoist is compact, lightweight, and has a simple structure, making it ideal for spaces with limited room. It is also easy to operate and control.</li>
              <li>Lower Cost: The manufacturing and maintenance costs of hoist-type cranes are relatively low, making them an ideal choice for small and medium-sized enterprises or projects with limited budgets.</li>
            </ul>
